data: {"type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT", "timestamp": 1793768071145, "messageId": "6676987195", "delta": "I recommend **1 doublet at 3,000 m, gas boiler top-up, electric chillers, sized so that any one unit can be out (N-1): boiler and chillers in equal units** (A1 · 1D-BO-EC@3000-N1-FC), the best overall: a reliable plan (any one unit can be out and every day is still met) and, of those, the cheapest when CO₂ counts at 137 €/t (the long-term price). It meets heat at 100 °C and cold at 20 °C every day of 2027 for 55.1 €/MWh of heat and cold together (heat 61.9 €/MWh, cold 23.5 €/MWh), with 63.8% less CO₂ than gas boilers and electric chillers, and passes all 14 checks. Its heat: the geothermal exchanger 68.4%, the heat pump 0%, the gas boiler 31.6% (it burns the produced gas first and buys 26.9 GWh of gas a year)."}

data: {"type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_END", "timestamp": 1793768071145, "messageId": "6676987195"}

